<title>USA: Armstrong, Worthington to build plant.</title>
<headline>Armstrong, Worthington to build plant.</headline>
<dateline>LANCASTER, Pa. 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Armstrong World Industries said Monday it plans to build a new manufacturing plant for WAVE, its ceiling grid joint venture with Worthington Industries Inc.</p>
<p>The plant will be located in Benton Harbor, Michigan, and should start up operations in the first half of 1998.</p>
<p>Armstrong declined to comment on the amount of money being invested in the project.</p>
<p>Formed in 1992, WAVE has plants in Nevada, France and Shanghai.</p>
